  honestNote:
    'The letter, its date, the reply and its date are printed in Price’s Vol. 2. The words of the letter belong to the Dake family, not to Price, and are attributed to them. Price prints what the 1997 edition changed: the section title became 30 reasons nations separated, intermarriage replaced miscegenation, and 19 uses of segregation remained in the concordance index; he leaves the reader to judge whether that went far enough. By his account the family never met with him and never answered his recall proposal. The figure of 35 years is his count from the 1963 first edition. The family’s own statement that Finis Dake attended and preached in Black churches is their testimony, recorded as theirs.',
